                            10
                            <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">اِسْتَنْقَى</span></b> 
                        
                        <i>He took extraordinary pains,</i> or
<i>the utmost pains, in cleansing his body.</i> (Mgh.)
You say also, <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">اِسْتَنْقَى الذَّكَرَ مِنَ البَوْلِ</span> (K, art.
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">برأ</span>,) [<i>He took extraordinary pains in cleansing
the</i>
                        <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">ذَكَر</span>
                        <i>from urine:</i> or] <i>he cleansed the</i>
                        <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">ذكر</span>
                        <i>entirely from urine;</i> syn. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">اِسْتَنْظَفَهُ</span>. (TA in that
art.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">اِسْتِنْقَاءٌ</span>: see voce <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">اِسْتَبْرَأَ</span>.

